      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't think this is really necessary... \nIf someone is open to criticism or looking for help, they can leave a sign up in their world with their discord or email or something.. Some even have their discord in their status when you view their profile when checking the world's creator... \nThousands of people use VRChat and if every person who joins a world could leave a comment or multiple comments, imagine how many notifications and spam just 1 person would receive. Now imagine if they had more than 1 world... Tbh, I'd rather just delete my worlds.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-01-21T21:47:01.859Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think this is pretty self explanatory but this is something I've wanted to be able to do for a while and especially after today. \nI was world hopping and came across a world that seemed promising and was about 90mb (mind you I dont have good internet so i was waiting quite a while), it was a pretty basic world and it had a bed and some couches and some other stuff that I dont even think loli sized avatars could \"fit\", they were just tiny. \nSo the ability to leave **constructive criticism/comments** on specifically community labs worlds just to help out the creator with maybe something they missed and didn't notice or didn't know how to do would be a pretty nice addition",
